FALLBACK ONLY -- do not apply unless the on-board DAC check fails.
Evidence says it should not be needed: /init.rc "on boot" does
  chown system system /sys/class/leds/lcd-backlight/brightness
(fix3p ramdisk init.rc:651) and the light service runs as user system
(android.hardware.light@2.0-service.rc:4).  LED class attributes are 0644,
so owner system can write.

If a board check shows "-rw-r--r-- root root" instead, either fix init.rc or
make the service root.  Root variant of /vendor/etc/init/android.hardware.light@2.0-service.rc:

 service vendor.light-hal-2-0 /vendor/bin/hw/android.hardware.light@2.0-service
     interface android.hardware.light@2.0::ILight default
     class hal
-    user system
-    group system
+    user root
+    group root
     shutdown critical
